cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fortranspire: LLM + MCP pipeline porting legacy Fortran HPC kernels to OpenACC GPU and differentiable JAX"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Loïc"
    family-names: "Maurin"
    email: "maurin.loic.ac@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8117-4850"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Toulouse, France"
abstract: >-
  fortranspire is an open-source Model Context Protocol (MCP) server and
  command-line agent that incrementally transforms legacy Fortran 90
  scientific code into GPU-accelerated (OpenACC), Python-callable
  (Cython / scikit-build), and optionally differentiable (JAX) form. It
  combines deterministic Loki AST analysis with targeted LLM calls
  against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Mistral La Plateforme,
  self-hosted vLLM / TGI / Ollama), so the agent stays sovereign and
  endpoint-agnostic.
